      <p>Both are extra-hot at 50,000–70,000 SHU. Jixin is a small heart-shaped pod from Guizhou and Hunan, the standard for extreme-heat products and Sichuan-style dishes; Xiaomi is a small, slender pod from Yunnan and Guizhou whose compact size keeps it visible whole in dishes or as segments.</p>
    </div>
